{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1779743658,"nonce":"gg8nlcXCW0QrEYApcJwiGYOxuyA=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABDnFUuQ","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/168#issuecomment-4537275577"},"message":"## Survey efficiency — analysis complete\n\nPart of the #169 post-mission analysis (combines §6 survey patterns with the #167 energy model). The 2026-05-22 mission re-ran the **same box 23×** (battery-drain test), so raw mission coverage is redundant — the intrinsic **per-pass** rate is the right metric.\n\n**Measured (representative 8-line pass, 18:22–18:28):** 3,181 m² in 6.6 min, 567 m track @ ~1.43 m/s, ~5.6 m effective swath, ~120 Wh (±30%) → **~29,000 m²/hr (2.9 ha/hr)**, **~27 m²/Wh**.\n\n**Coverage scales with line spacing** (area/charge ∝ spacing), @1.5 m/s:\n\n| Spacing | Rate | /charge (ideal) | derated ~80% |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 m | ~5,400 m²/hr | ~3.3 ha | ~2.7 ha |\n| 2 m | ~10,800 m²/hr | ~6.7 ha | ~5.3 ha |\n| ~5.6 m | ~29,000 m²/hr | ~18.6 ha | ~15 ha |\n| 10 m | ~51,000 m²/hr | ~33 ha | ~26 ha |\n\n**Levers (for class-prep planning):**\n- **Line spacing dominates** area-per-charge — survey at the widest spacing the sonar swath allows; don't over-sample (the 1–2 m test spacing yields only ~3–7 ha/charge).\n- **Short lines (58 m) cost efficiency** (turn overhead per area); longer lines amortize turns.\n- Energy is ±30% (no current sensor, per #167); coverage assumes spacing = effective swath.\n\nFull write-up in the deployment analysis (to land in the consolidated #169 PR). Closing — analysis done.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":4,"timestamp":1779743659,"nonce":"E4G+xrlEVlT91hgi6TKfv6tTSYY=","metadata":{"github-id":"CE_lADOK4fCvM8AAAABDJ7Jus8AAAAGCigQjw"},"status":2},{"type":4,"timestamp":1779744274,"nonce":"LmbkiqxafklmOfTu3AQUEY19WEk=","metadata":{"github-id":"REE_lADOK4fCvM8AAAABDJ7Jus8AAAAGCiuw_Q"},"status":1},{"type":3,"timestamp":1779744275,"nonce":"C7YIEU55Cjepxhb4O4XoysGg5e0=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABDnImeg","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/168#issuecomment-4537329274"},"message":"## Correction — coverage is governed by sonar swath, not the lines flown\n\nMy earlier comment anchored coverage on the mission's **line spacing**, but that geometry (tight ~1–6 m spacing, short 58 m lines, same box re-run 23×) was a **battery-drain-while-staying-near-the-pier** choice — *not* survey spacing. So it doesn't represent survey coverage, and the per-spacing numbers under-stated real coverage ~10–20×.\n\n**Correct framing:** the boat's transferable contribution is **track-distance per charge** (= #167 range): ~40 km @ 1.5 m/s ideal, **~32 km de-rated**. **Survey coverage = track × sonar swath**, where the swath is the M3 multibeam's across-track coverage (∝ water depth × beam angle) — a sonar/depth parameter, *not* a power one, and not determined by this mission.\n\nCoverage per charge (de-rated ~32 km track @ 1.5 m/s), by swath:\n\n| Sonar swath | Rate @1.5 m/s | Area / charge |\n|---|---|---|\n| 5 m | ~2.7 ha/hr | ~16 ha |\n| 10 m | ~5.4 ha/hr | ~32 ha |\n| 20 m | ~11 ha/hr | ~64 ha |\n| 40 m | ~22 ha/hr | ~128 ha |\n\n**Levers (in order):** (1) sonar swath (∝ depth — use the widest the sonar/depth gives), (2) track-distance per charge (#167), (3) longer lines to amortize turns. Determining the actual M3 swath at survey depth is a separate sonar analysis.\n\nUpdated write-up in the deployment analysis (to land in the consolidated #169 PR). Re-closing with the corrected framing.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":4,"timestamp":1779744276,"nonce":"GD895cHA3KtXcO/l6irXw7tGaWg=","metadata":{"github-id":"CE_lADOK4fCvM8AAAABDJ7Jus8AAAAGCiu11w"},"status":2}]}